# ============================================================================
# Tech Monster — CODEOWNERS
# ============================================================================
#
# Purpose:
#   This file defines the default reviewers/owners for different areas of the
#   Tech Monster repository.
#
# How CODEOWNERS works:
#   - Each rule contains a file/folder pattern followed by one or more owners.
#   - When a pull request modifies a matching path, GitHub can request review
#     from the configured owners.
#   - More specific rules should be placed after broader rules because the
#     last matching pattern takes precedence.
#
# Important:
#   Replace the placeholder GitHub team/user handles below with the actual
#   maintainers before enabling mandatory CODEOWNERS approval rules.
#
# Documentation:
#   https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
# ============================================================================


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default Repository Ownership
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Use this as the fallback owner for files that do not match a more specific
# rule below.
#
# Example:
#   * @Tech-Monster-Dev/maintainers
#
# Uncomment and configure this once the organization has a dedicated
# maintainers/reviewers team.
#
# * @Tech-Monster-Dev/maintainers


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The backend contains the server-side application, APIs, business logic,
# security middleware, validation, infrastructure integrations, and data
# processing.
#
# Backend changes should be reviewed by developers responsible for the
# server-side architecture and API contracts.
#
# Configure the appropriate GitHub team before enabling these rules.
#
# /backend/ @Tech-Monster-Dev/backend-maintainers


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The frontend contains the client application, UI components, pages,
# routing, state management, API integration, styling, and user-facing
# functionality.
#
# Frontend changes should be reviewed by developers responsible for the
# frontend architecture and user experience.
#
# Configure the appropriate GitHub team before enabling these rules.
#
# /frontend/ @Tech-Monster-Dev/frontend-maintainers


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend API / Application Entry Points
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Changes to core backend application initialization can affect the complete
# API lifecycle and therefore deserve additional architectural review.
#
# /backend/src/app.js @Tech-Monster-Dev/backend-maintainers


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend Core
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Core modules usually contain cross-cutting infrastructure such as:
#   - Error handling
#   - Authentication
#   - Authorization
#   - Rate limiting
#   - Validation
#   - HTTP helpers
#
# Changes here can affect many API modules, so they should be reviewed
# carefully.
#
# /backend/src/core/ @Tech-Monster-Dev/backend-maintainers


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Documentation changes normally do not require application-code ownership,
# but assigning them to maintainers helps ensure that architecture,
# development instructions, API documentation, and deployment procedures
# remain accurate.
#
# /docs/ @Tech-Monster-Dev/maintainers


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repository Automation
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Changes to GitHub Actions, issue templates, pull-request templates, or
# repository ownership rules can affect the development workflow itself.
#
# These files should be reviewed by repository maintainers.
#
# /.github/ @Tech-Monster-Dev/maintainers


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI/CD Workflows
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Workflow changes can affect automated testing, linting, validation,
# deployment, and security checks.
#
# /.github/workflows/ @Tech-Monster-Dev/maintainers


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Development and Maintenance Scripts
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Scripts can modify project state, automate maintenance tasks, or influence
# development workflows. Review them before merging changes.
#
# /scripts/ @Tech-Monster-Dev/maintainers


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependency and Package Configuration
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Dependency changes can introduce security, compatibility, performance, or
# licensing implications.
#
# Backend package configuration:
#
# /backend/package.json @Tech-Monster-Dev/backend-maintainers
# /backend/package-lock.json @Tech-Monster-Dev/backend-maintainers
#
# Frontend package configuration:
#
# /frontend/package.json @Tech-Monster-Dev/frontend-maintainers
# /frontend/package-lock.json @Tech-Monster-Dev/frontend-maintainers


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Security-Sensitive Configuration
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Authentication, authorization, validation, rate limiting, and security
# configuration changes should receive explicit backend/security review.
#
# These rules can be enabled once the corresponding GitHub team exists.
#
# /backend/src/core/security/ @Tech-Monster-Dev/security-maintainers


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repository-Wide Configuration
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Changes to these files can affect every developer or every part of the
# application and should therefore be reviewed by repository maintainers.
#
# /.editorconfig @Tech-Monster-Dev/maintainers
# /.gitignore @Tech-Monster-Dev/maintainers
# /.hintrc @Tech-Monster-Dev/maintainers
# /CONTRIBUTING.md @Tech-Monster-Dev/maintainers
# /LICENSE @Tech-Monster-Dev/maintainers
# /README.md @Tech-Monster-Dev/maintainers


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Future Ownership Rules
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# As the project grows, introduce more specific ownership rules for major
# domains rather than assigning every file to one person.
#
# Recommended ownership model:
#
#   1. Repository Maintainers
#      Own global configuration, documentation, CI/CD, and project policy.
#
#   2. Frontend Maintainers
#      Own React/UI architecture and client-side application code.
#
#   3. Backend Maintainers
#      Own APIs, services, persistence, authentication, and server-side code.
#
#   4. Security Maintainers
#      Review authentication, authorization, secrets handling, validation,
#      rate limiting, and other security-sensitive changes.
#
#   5. Documentation Maintainers
#      Keep developer documentation, API documentation, and architecture
#      documentation synchronized with the implementation.
#
# Avoid assigning every path to an individual developer unless that person is
# expected to remain responsible for the area. Prefer GitHub teams for long-
# lived ownership because teams scale better as contributors change.
# ============================================================================